      (twin5_slice.json absent; skipping)

scope
-----
Proved here: (BC) is necessary; (BC) contains both Lemma-1 cuts and
vertex Hall; (BC) can fire exactly for k in {8,10,12,14} and never
at k = 16; vertex Hall never fires for n >= 11; (BC) is NOT
sufficient at n = 7 or 9, and the fractional relaxation is not
sufficient at n = 7.  NOT proved here: that every class-B or
class-B' instance completes at n = 13, that a simultaneous fan or an
LS(3,4,20) exists, or anything about Erdos-Rosenfeld Problem #835,
which remains open.
